\s1 Ruth’s Loyalty to Naomi
\p \v 6 \rb When|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb Naomi heard|שָֽׁמְעָה֙\rb*\rb |בִּשְׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb in Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had attended to|פָקַ֤ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His people|עַמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb by providing|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb with food,|לָֽחֶם׃\rb* \rb she|הִיא֙\rb* \rb and her daughters-in-law|וְכַלֹּתֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb prepared|וַתָּ֤קָם\rb* \rb to leave|וַתָּ֖שָׁב\rb* \rb the land|מִשְּׂדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Moab.|מוֹאָ֑ב\rb* \v 7 \rb Accompanied by|עִמָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb her two|וּשְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb daughters-in-law,|כַלֹּתֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb she left|וַתֵּצֵ֗א\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּקוֹם֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb she had been living|הָיְתָה־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔מָּה\rb* \rb and set out|וַתֵּלַ֣כְנָה\rb* \rb on the road|בַדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb leading back|לָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*
