\p \rb And she kissed|וַתִּשַּׁ֣ק\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֔ן\rb* \rb as they wept|וַתִּבְכֶּֽינָה׃\rb* \rb aloud|וַתִּשֶּׂ֥אנָה\rb*\rb |קוֹלָ֖ן\rb* \v 10 \rb and said,|וַתֹּאמַ֖רְנָה־\rb* \rb “Surely|כִּי־\rb* \rb we will return|נָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb to your people.”|לְעַמֵּֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb But Naomi|נָעֳמִי֙\rb* \rb replied,|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb “Return home,|שֹׁ֣בְנָה\rb* \rb my daughters.|בְנֹתַ֔י\rb* \rb Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb would you go|תֵלַ֖כְנָה\rb* \rb with me?|עִמִּ֑י\rb* \rb Are there still|הַֽעֽוֹד־\rb* \rb sons|בָנִים֙\rb*\rb |לִ֤י\rb* \rb in my womb|בְּֽמֵעַ֔י\rb* \rb to become|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb husbands?|לַאֲנָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Return home,|שֹׁ֤בְנָה\rb* \rb my daughters.|בְנֹתַי֙\rb* \rb Go on,|לֵ֔כְןָ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I am too old|זָקַ֖נְתִּי\rb* \rb to have|מִהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb another husband.|לְאִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb Even if|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I thought|אָמַ֙רְתִּי֙\rb* \rb there was|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb hope|תִקְוָ֔ה\rb* \rb for me|לִ֣י\rb* \rb to have|הָיִ֤יתִי\rb* \rb a husband|לְאִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |וְגַ֖ם\rb* \rb tonight|הַלַּ֙יְלָה֙\rb* \rb and|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb to bear|יָלַ֥דְתִּי\rb* \rb sons,|בָנִֽים׃\rb* \v 13 \rb would you wait|תְּשַׂבֵּ֗רְנָה\rb* \rb for them|הֲלָהֵ֣ן׀\rb* \rb to|עַ֚ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb grow up?|יִגְדָּ֔לוּ\rb*\rb |הֲלָהֵן֙\rb* \rb Would you refrain|תֵּֽעָגֵ֔נָה\rb* \rb from|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb having|הֱי֣וֹת\rb* \rb husbands?|לְאִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb No,|אַ֣ל\rb* \rb my daughters,|בְּנֹתַ֗י\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it is much more bitter|מַר־\rb*\rb |מְאֹד֙\rb* \rb for me|לִ֤י\rb* \rb than for you,|מִכֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb has gone out|יָצְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb against me.”|בִ֖י\rb*
