\p \v 20 \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb call|תִּקְרֶ֥אנָה\rb* \rb me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb Naomi,|נָעֳמִ֑י\rb*\f + \fr 1:20 \fqa Naomi \ft means \fqa pleasant\ft .\f*” \rb she replied.|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֔ן\rb* \rb “Call|קְרֶ֤אןָ\rb* \rb me|לִי֙\rb* \rb Mara,|מָרָ֔א\rb*\f + \fr 1:20 \fqa Mara \ft means \fqa bitter\ft .\f* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb the Almighty|שַׁדַּ֛י\rb*\f + \fr 1:20 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shaddai\ft ; also in verse 21\f* \rb has dealt quite bitterly|הֵמַ֥ר\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb with me.|לִ֖י\rb* \v 21 \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb went away|הָלַ֔כְתִּי\rb* \rb full,|מְלֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb but the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb has brought me back|הֱשִׁיבַ֣נִי\rb* \rb empty.|וְרֵיקָ֖ם\rb* \rb Why|לָ֣מָּה\rb* \rb call|תִקְרֶ֤אנָה\rb* \rb me|לִי֙\rb* \rb Naomi?|נָעֳמִ֔י\rb* \rb After all, the LORD|וַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb has testified|עָ֣נָה\rb* \rb against me,|בִ֔י\rb* \rb and the Almighty|וְשַׁדַּ֖י\rb* \rb has afflicted|הֵ֥רַֽע\rb* \rb me.”|לִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb So Naomi|נָעֳמִ֗י\rb* \rb returned|וַתָּ֣שָׁב\rb* \rb from the land|מִשְּׂדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֑ב\rb* \rb with|עִמָּ֔הּ\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁ֖בָה\rb* \rb her daughter-in-law|כַלָּתָהּ֙\rb* \rb Ruth|וְר֨וּת\rb* \rb the Moabitess.|הַמּוֹאֲבִיָּ֤ה\rb* \rb And they|וְהֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb arrived|בָּ֚אוּ\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb in Bethlehem|לֶ֔חֶם\rb* \rb at the beginning|בִּתְחִלַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of the barley|שְׂעֹרִֽים׃\rb* \rb harvest.|קְצִ֥יר\rb*
\c 2
\s1 Boaz Meets Ruth
\p \v 1 \rb Now Naomi|וּֽלְנָעֳמִ֞י\rb* \rb had a relative|מְיֻדָּע\rb* \rb on her husband’s side,|לְאִישָׁ֗הּ\rb* \rb a prominent|גִּבּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb man|אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb of noble character|חַ֔יִל\rb* \rb from the clan|מִמִּשְׁפַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb of Elimelech,|אֱלִימֶ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb whose name|וּשְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb was Boaz.|בֹּֽעַז׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb And Ruth|ר֨וּת\rb* \rb the Moabitess|הַמּוֹאֲבִיָּ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to Naomi,|נָעֳמִ֗י\rb* \rb “Please|נָּ֤א\rb* \rb let me go|אֵֽלְכָה־\rb* \rb into the fields|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \rb and glean|וַאֲלַקֳטָּ֣ה\rb* \rb heads of grain|בַשִׁבֳּלִ֔ים\rb* \rb after someone|אַחַ֕ר\rb* \rb in whose|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb sight|בְּעֵינָ֑יו\rb* \rb I may find|אֶמְצָא־\rb* \rb favor.”|חֵ֖ן\rb*
\p \rb “Go ahead,|לְכִ֥י\rb* \rb my daughter,”|בִתִּֽי׃\rb* \rb Naomi replied.|וַתֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb So Ruth departed|וַתֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb and went out|וַתָּבוֹא֙\rb* \rb into the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and gleaned|וַתְּלַקֵּ֣ט\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the harvesters.|הַקֹּצְרִ֑ים\rb* \rb And she happened|וַיִּ֣קֶר\rb* \rb to come|מִקְרֶ֔הָ\rb* \rb to the part|חֶלְקַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \rb belonging to Boaz,|לְבֹ֔עַז\rb* \rb who was|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb from the clan|מִמִּשְׁפַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb of Elimelech.|אֱלִימֶֽלֶךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Just then|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb Boaz|בֹ֗עַז\rb* \rb arrived|בָּ֚א\rb* \rb from|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Bethlehem|לֶ֔חֶם\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to the harvesters,|לַקּוֹצְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb “The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb be with you.”|עִמָּכֶ֑ם\rb*
\p \rb “The LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb bless you,”|יְבָרֶכְךָ֥\rb* \rb they replied.|וַיֹּ֥אמְרוּ\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb And Boaz|בֹּ֙עַז֙\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the foreman|לְנַעֲר֔וֹ\rb*\rb |הַנִּצָּ֖ב\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb his harvesters,|הַקּֽוֹצְרִ֑ים\rb* \rb “Whose|לְמִ֖י\rb* \rb young woman|הַנַּעֲרָ֥ה\rb* \rb is this?”|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb The foreman|הַנַּ֛עַר\rb*\rb |הַנִּצָּ֥ב\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |הַקּוֹצְרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb answered,|וַיַּ֗עַן\rb* \rb “She is|הִ֔יא\rb* \rb the Moabitess|מֽוֹאֲבִיָּה֙\rb*\rb |נַעֲרָ֤ה\rb* \rb who returned|הַשָּׁ֥בָה\rb* \rb with|עִֽם־\rb* \rb Naomi|נָעֳמִ֖י\rb* \rb from the land|מִשְּׂדֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of Moab.|מוֹאָֽב׃\rb* \v 7 \rb She has said,|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb ‘Please|נָּא֙\rb* \rb let me glean|אֲלַקֳטָה־\rb* \rb and gather|וְאָסַפְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb among the sheaves|בָֽעֳמָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the harvesters.’|הַקּוֹצְרִ֑ים\rb* \rb So she came out|וַתָּב֣וֹא\rb* \rb and has continued|וַֽתַּעֲמ֗וֹד\rb* \rb from|מֵאָ֤ז\rb* \rb morning|הַבֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb* \rb until|וְעַד־\rb* \rb now,|עַ֔תָּה\rb* \rb except|זֶ֛ה\rb* \rb that she rested|שִׁבְתָּ֥הּ\rb* \rb a short time|מְעָֽט׃\rb* \rb in the shelter.”|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Then Boaz|בֹּ֨עַז\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ruth,|ר֜וּת\rb* \rb |הֲל֧וֹא\rb* \rb “Listen,|שָׁמַ֣עַתְּ\rb* \rb my daughter.|בִּתִּ֗י\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb go|תֵּלְכִי֙\rb* \rb and glean|לִלְקֹט֙\rb* \rb in another|אַחֵ֔ר\rb* \rb field,|בְּשָׂדֶ֣ה\rb* \rb and|וְגַ֛ם\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb go away|תַעֲבוּרִ֖י\rb* \rb from this place,|מִזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb but stay here|וְכֹ֥ה\rb* \rb close|תִדְבָּקִ֖ין\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb my servant girls.|נַעֲרֹתָֽי׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Let your eyes be on|עֵינַ֜יִךְ\rb* \rb the|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֤ה\rb* \rb they are harvesting,|יִקְצֹרוּן֙\rb* \rb and follow along|וְהָלַ֣כְתִּ\rb* \rb after these girls.|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֔ן\rb* \rb Indeed,|הֲל֥וֹא\rb* \rb I have ordered|צִוִּ֛יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the young men|הַנְּעָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb not|לְבִלְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb to touch you.|נָגְעֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb And when you are thirsty,|וְצָמִ֗ת\rb* \rb go|וְהָלַכְתְּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb and drink|וְשָׁתִ֕ית\rb* \rb from|מֵאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the jars|הַכֵּלִ֔ים\rb* \rb the young men|הַנְּעָרִֽים׃\rb* \rb have filled.”|יִשְׁאֲב֖וּן\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb At this, she fell|וַתִּפֹּל֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb her face,|פָּנֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb bowing low|וַתִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb to the ground,|אָ֑רְצָה\rb* \rb and said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb “Why|מַדּוּעַ֩\rb* \rb have I found|מָצָ֨אתִי\rb* \rb such favor|חֵ֤ן\rb* \rb in your eyes|בְּעֵינֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb that you should take notice of me,|לְהַכִּירֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb even though I am|וְאָּנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb a foreigner?”|נָכְרִיָּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Boaz|בֹּ֙עַז֙\rb* \rb replied,|וַיַּ֤עַן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |לָ֔הּ\rb* \rb “I have been made fully aware|הֻגֵּ֨ד\rb*\rb |הֻגַּ֜ד\rb*\rb |לִ֗י\rb* \rb of all|כֹּ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have done|עָשִׂית֙\rb* \rb for|אֶת־\rb* \rb your mother-in-law|חֲמוֹתֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb since|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb the death|מ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of your husband,|אִישֵׁ֑ךְ\rb* \rb how you left|וַתַּֽעַזְבִ֞י\rb* \rb your father|אָּבִ֣יךְ\rb* \rb and mother|וְאִמֵּ֗ךְ\rb* \rb and the land|וְאֶ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb of your birth,|מֽוֹלַדְתֵּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and how you came|וַתֵּ֣לְכִ֔י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a people|עַ֕ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֖עַתְּ\rb* \rb before.|תְּמ֥וֹל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֽׁוֹם׃\rb* \v 12 \rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb repay|יְשַׁלֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb your work,|פָּעֳלֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb and may you receive|וּתְהִ֨י\rb* \rb a rich|שְׁלֵמָ֗ה\rb* \rb reward|מַשְׂכֻּרְתֵּ֜ךְ\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֤ם\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb under|תַּֽחַת־\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb wings|כְּנָפָֽיו׃\rb* \rb you have taken|בָּ֖את\rb* \rb refuge.”|לַחֲס֥וֹת\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb “My lord,”|אֲדֹנִי֙\rb* \rb she said,|וַ֠תֹּאמֶר\rb* \rb “may I continue to find|אֶמְצָא־\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֨ן\rb* \rb in your eyes,|בְּעֵינֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have comforted|נִֽחַמְתָּ֔נִי\rb*\rb |וְכִ֥י\rb* \rb and spoken|דִבַּ֖רְתָּ\rb* \rb kindly|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb your maidservant,|שִׁפְחָתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb though I|וְאָנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb am|אֶֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb like one|כְּאַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb of your servant girls.”|שִׁפְחֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb At mealtime|לְעֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |הָאֹ֗כֶל\rb* \rb Boaz|בֹ֜עַז\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to her,|לָ֨ה\rb* \rb “Come over|גֹּ֤שִֽׁי\rb* \rb here;|הֲלֹם֙\rb* \rb have|וְאָכַ֣לְתְּ\rb* \rb some|מִן־\rb* \rb bread|הַלֶּ֔חֶם\rb* \rb and dip|וְטָבַ֥לְתְּ\rb* \rb it|פִּתֵּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb into the vinegar sauce.”|בַּחֹ֑מֶץ\rb* \rb So she sat down|וַתֵּ֙שֶׁב֙\rb* \rb beside|מִצַּ֣ד\rb* \rb the harvesters,|הַקּֽוֹצְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and he offered|וַיִּצְבָּט־\rb* \rb her|לָ֣הּ\rb* \rb roasted grain,|קָלִ֔י\rb* \rb and she ate|וַתֹּ֥אכַל\rb* \rb and was satisfied|וַתִּשְׂבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb and had some left over.|וַתֹּתַֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb When Ruth got up|וַתָּ֖קָם\rb* \rb to glean,|לְלַקֵּ֑ט\rb* \rb Boaz|בֹּ֨עַז\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb ordered|וַיְצַו֩\rb* \rb his young men,|נְעָרָ֜יו\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb “Even if|גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb she gathers|תְּלַקֵּ֖ט\rb* \rb among|בֵּ֧ין\rb* \rb the sheaves,|הָֽעֳמָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb insult her.|תַכְלִימֽוּהָ׃\rb* \v 16 \rb Rather,|וְגַ֛ם\rb* \rb pull out|שֹׁל־\rb*\rb |תָּשֹׁ֥לּוּ\rb* \rb for her|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb some stalks from|מִן־\rb* \rb the bundles|הַצְּבָתִ֑ים\rb* \rb and leave them|וַעֲזַבְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb for her to gather.|וְלִקְּטָ֖ה\rb* \rb Do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb rebuke|תִגְעֲרוּ־\rb* \rb her.”|בָֽהּ׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb So Ruth gathered grain|וַתְּלַקֵּ֥ט\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening.|הָעָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb And when she beat out|וַתַּחְבֹּט֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she had gleaned,|לִקֵּ֔טָה\rb* \rb it was|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb about an ephah|כְּאֵיפָ֥ה\rb* \rb of barley.|שְׂעֹרִֽים׃\rb*\f + \fr 2:17 \fqa An ephah \ft is approximately 20 dry quarts or 22 liters (probably about 29 pounds or 13.2 kilograms of barley).\f* \v 18 \rb She picked up the grain|וַתִּשָּׂא֙\rb* \rb and went into|וַתָּב֣וֹא\rb* \rb the town,|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb where her mother-in-law|חֲמוֹתָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb saw|וַתֵּ֥רֶא\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she had gleaned.|לִקֵּ֑טָה\rb* \rb And she brought out|וַתּוֹצֵא֙\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she had saved|הוֹתִ֖רָה\rb* \rb from her meal|מִשָּׂבְעָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb and gave it|וַתִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb to Naomi.|לָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Then her mother-in-law|חֲמוֹתָ֜הּ\rb* \rb asked|וַתֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb her,|לָ֨הּ\rb* \rb “Where|אֵיפֹ֨ה\rb* \rb did you glean|לִקַּ֤טְתְּ\rb* \rb today,|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb and where|וְאָ֣נָה\rb* \rb did you work?|עָשִׂ֔ית\rb* \rb Blessed|בָּר֑וּךְ\rb* \rb be the man|יְהִ֥י\rb* \rb who noticed you.”|מַכִּירֵ֖ךְ\rb*
\p \rb So she told|וַתַּגֵּ֣ד\rb* \rb her mother-in-law|לַחֲמוֹתָ֗הּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she had worked.|עָשְׂתָה֙\rb*\rb |עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb “The name|שֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb of the man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I worked|עָשִׂ֧יתִי\rb* \rb with|עִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb is Boaz,”|בֹּֽעַז׃\rb* \rb she said.|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb Then Naomi|נָעֳמִ֜י\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to her daughter-in-law,|לְכַלָּתָ֗הּ\rb* \rb “May he|הוּא֙\rb* \rb be blessed|בָּר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb by the LORD,|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb has not|לֹא־\rb* \rb withdrawn|עָזַ֣ב\rb* \rb His kindness|חַסְדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb from|אֶת־\rb* \rb the living|הַחַיִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb or the dead.”|הַמֵּתִ֑ים\rb* \rb Naomi|נָעֳמִ֗י\rb* \rb continued,|וַתֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb “The man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb is a close relative.|קָר֥וֹב\rb* \rb He|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is one of our|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb kinsman-redeemers.|מִֽגֹּאֲלֵ֖נוּ\rb*\f + \fr 2:20 \ft The Hebrew word for \fqa kinsman-redeemer \ft or \fqa guardian-redeemer\ft is a legal term for the kinsman who redeems or vindicates a relative; see \ref Leviticus 25:25–55|LEV 25:25-55\ref*.\f*”
\p \v 21 \rb Then Ruth|ר֣וּת\rb* \rb the Moabitess|הַמּוֹאֲבִיָּ֑ה\rb* \rb said,|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “He also|גַּ֣ם׀\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb told me,|אָמַ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb ‘Stay|תִּדְבָּקִ֔ין\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb my young men|הַנְּעָרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |לִי֙\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb they have finished gathering|כִּלּ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my|לִֽי׃\rb* \rb harvest.’”|הַקָּצִ֖יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb And Naomi|נָעֳמִ֖י\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb her daughter-in-law|כַּלָּתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb Ruth,|ר֣וּת\rb* \rb “My daughter,|בִּתִּ֗י\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb it is good|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb for you to work|תֵֽצְאִי֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his young women,|נַ֣עֲרוֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb so that nothing|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb will happen|יִפְגְּעוּ־\rb* \rb to you|בָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in another|אַחֵֽר׃\rb* \rb field.”|בְּשָׂדֶ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb So Ruth stayed close|וַתִּדְבַּ֞ק\rb* \rb to the servant girls|בְּנַעֲר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Boaz|בֹּ֙עַז֙\rb* \rb to glean|לְלַקֵּ֔ט\rb* \rb grain until|עַד־\rb* \rb the barley|הַשְּׂעֹרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וּקְצִ֣יר\rb* \rb and wheat|הַֽחִטִּ֑ים\rb* \rb harvests|קְצִֽיר־\rb* \rb were finished.|כְּל֥וֹת\rb* \rb And she lived|וַתֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb her mother-in-law.|חֲמוֹתָֽהּ׃\rb*
\c 3
\s1 Ruth’s Redemption Assured
\p \v 1 \rb One day Ruth’s mother-in-law|חֲמוֹתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb Naomi|נָעֳמִ֣י\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to her,|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb “My daughter,|בִּתִּ֞י\rb* \rb should I not|הֲלֹ֧א\rb* \rb seek|אֲבַקֶּשׁ־\rb* \rb a resting place|מָנ֖וֹחַ\rb* \rb for you,|לָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb it may be well|יִֽיטַב־\rb* \rb with you?|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb is not|הֲלֹ֥א\rb* \rb Boaz,|בֹ֙עַז֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb servant girls|נַעֲרוֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb you have been working,|הָיִ֖ית\rb* \rb a relative of ours?|מֹֽדַעְתָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb In fact,|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb tonight|הַלָּֽיְלָה׃\rb* \rb he|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb is winnowing|זֹרֶ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb barley|הַשְּׂעֹרִ֖ים\rb* \rb on the threshing floor.|גֹּ֥רֶן\rb* \v 3 \rb Therefore wash yourself,|וְרָחַ֣צְתְּ׀\rb* \rb put on perfume,|וָסַ֗כְתְּ\rb* \rb and wear|וְשַׂ֧מְתְּ\rb* \rb your best clothes.|שִׂמְלֹתֵךְ\rb*\rb |עָלַ֖יִךְ\rb* \rb Go down|וְיָרַדְתִּי\rb* \rb to the threshing floor,|הַגֹּ֑רֶן\rb* \rb but do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let the man|לָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb know|תִּוָּדְעִ֣י\rb* \rb you are there until|עַ֥ד\rb* \rb he has finished|כַּלֹּת֖וֹ\rb* \rb eating|לֶאֱכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb and drinking.|וְלִשְׁתּֽוֹת׃\rb* \v 4 \rb |וִיהִ֣י\rb* \rb When he lies down,|בְשָׁכְב֗וֹ\rb* \rb note|וְיָדַ֙עַתְּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּקוֹם֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he lies.|יִשְׁכַּב־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb Then go in|וּבָ֛את\rb* \rb and uncover|וְגִלִּ֥ית\rb* \rb his feet,|מַרְגְּלֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb and lie down,|וְשָׁכָבְתִּי\rb* \rb and he|וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb will explain|יַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb to you|לָ֔ךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you should do.”|תַּעַשִֽׂין׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb “I will do|אֶֽעֱשֶֽׂה׃\rb* \rb everything|כֹּ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you say,”|תֹּאמְרִ֥יֵַ֖\rb* \rb Ruth answered.|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \v 6 \rb So she went down|וַתֵּ֖רֶד\rb* \rb to the threshing floor|הַגֹּ֑רֶן\rb* \rb and did|וַתַּ֕עַשׂ\rb* \rb everything|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb her mother-in-law|חֲמוֹתָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb had instructed her to do.|צִוַּ֖תָּה\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb After Boaz|בֹּ֤עַז\rb* \rb had finished eating|וַיֹּ֨אכַל\rb* \rb and drinking|וַיֵּשְׁתְּ֙\rb* \rb and was in good spirits,|וַיִּיטַ֣ב\rb*\rb |לִבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb he went|וַיָּבֹ֕א\rb* \rb to lie down|לִשְׁכַּ֖ב\rb* \rb at the end|בִּקְצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the heap of grain.|הָעֲרֵמָ֑ה\rb* \rb Then Ruth went in secretly,|וַתָּבֹ֣א\rb*\rb |בַלָּ֔ט\rb* \rb uncovered|וַתְּגַ֥ל\rb* \rb his feet,|מַרְגְּלֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb and lay down.|וַתִּשְׁכָּֽב׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb |וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb At midnight,|בַּחֲצִ֣י\rb*\rb |הַלַּ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb Boaz|הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb was startled,|וַיֶּחֱרַ֥ד\rb* \rb turned over,|וַיִּלָּפֵ֑ת\rb* \rb and there|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb lying|שֹׁכֶ֖בֶת\rb* \rb at his feet|מַרְגְּלֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb was a woman!|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb “Who|מִי־\rb* \rb are you?”|אָ֑תּ\rb* \rb he asked.|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*
\p \rb “I am|אָנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb your servant|אֲמָתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb Ruth,”|ר֣וּת\rb* \rb she replied.|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Spread|וּפָרַשְׂתָּ֤\rb* \rb the corner of your garment|כְנָפֶ֙ךָ֙\rb*\f + \fr 3:9 \ft Or \fqa Spread your wing\ft ; the word for \fqa wing \ft can also mean \fqa corner of a garment\ft ; see \ref Ruth 2:12|RUT 2:12\ref*.\f* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb me,|אֲמָ֣תְךָ֔\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אָֽתָּה׃\rb* \rb are a kinsman-redeemer.|גֹאֵ֖ל\rb*\f + \fr 3:9 \ft The Hebrew word for \fqa kinsman-redeemer \ft or \fqa guardian-redeemer\ft is a legal term for the kinsman who redeems or vindicates a relative; similarly in verses 12 and 13; see \ref Leviticus 25:25–55|LEV 25:25-55\ref*.\f*”
\p \v 10 \rb Then Boaz said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “May the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb bless|בְּרוּכָ֨ה\rb* \rb you,|אַ֤תְּ\rb* \rb my daughter.|בִּתִּ֔י\rb* \rb You have shown|הֵיטַ֛בְתְּ\rb* \rb more kindness|חַסְדֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb now|הָאַחֲר֖וֹן\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb before,|הָרִאשׁ֑וֹן\rb* \rb because you have not|לְבִלְתִּי־\rb* \rb run|לֶ֗כֶת\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb the younger men,|הַבַּ֣חוּרִ֔ים\rb* \rb whether|אִם־\rb* \rb rich|עָשִֽׁיר׃\rb* \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb poor.|דַּ֖ל\rb* \v 11 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid,|תִּ֣ירְאִ֔י\rb* \rb my daughter.|בִּתִּי֙\rb* \rb I will do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb for you|לָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb whatever|כֹּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you request,|תֹּאמְרִ֖י\rb* \rb since|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my fellow townspeople|עַמִּ֔י\rb*\rb |שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb know|יוֹדֵ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb you|אָֽתְּ׃\rb* \rb are a woman|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb of noble character.|חַ֖יִל\rb* \v 12 \rb |וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb Yes,|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb it is true|אָמְנָ֔ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I am|אָנֹ֑כִי\rb* \rb a kinsman-redeemer,|גֹאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb but|וְגַ֛ם\rb* \rb there is|יֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb a redeemer|גֹּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb nearer|קָר֥וֹב\rb* \rb than I.|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb*\f + \fr 3:12 \ft That is, more closely related\f* \v 13 \rb Stay here tonight,|לִ֣ינִי׀\rb*\rb |הַלַּ֗יְלָה\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb and in the morning,|בַבֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb he wants to redeem you,|יִגְאָלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb good.|טוֹב֙\rb* \rb Let him redeem you.|יִגְאָ֔ל\rb* \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb he does not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb want|יַחְפֹּ֧ץ\rb* \rb to redeem you,|לְגָֽאֳלֵ֛ךְ\rb* \rb as surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb lives,|חַי־\rb* \rb I|אָנֹ֖כִי\rb* \rb will.|וּגְאַלְתִּ֥יךְ\rb* \rb Now lie here|שִׁכְבִ֖י\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning.”|הַבֹּֽקֶר׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb So she lay down|וַתִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb at his feet|מַרְגְּלֹתָו\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning,|הַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb but she got up|וַתָּ֕קָם\rb* \rb before|בִּטְרוֹם\rb* \rb anyone|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb else|רֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb could recognize her.|יַכִּ֥יר\rb*
\p \rb Then Boaz said,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let it be known|יִוָּדַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb a woman|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb came|בָ֥אָה\rb* \rb to the threshing floor.”|הַגֹּֽרֶן׃\rb* \v 15 \rb And he told her,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Bring|הָ֠בִי\rb* \rb the shawl|הַמִּטְפַּ֧חַת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you are wearing|עָלַ֛יִךְ\rb* \rb and hold|וְאֶֽחֳזִי־\rb* \rb it out.”|בָ֖הּ\rb* \rb When she did so,|וַתֹּ֣אחֶז\rb*\rb |בָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb he poured in|וַיָּ֤מָד\rb* \rb six measures|שֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb of barley|שְׂעֹרִים֙\rb*\f + \fr 3:15 \ft Possibly six seahs (two ephahs), or approximately 39.6 dry quarts or 43.8 liters (about 58 pounds or 26.3 kilograms of barley) \f* \rb and placed it|וַיָּ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb on her.|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb Then he went|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb*\f + \fr 3:15 \ft Most Hebrew manuscripts; many Hebrew manuscripts, Vulgate, and Syriac \fqa she went\f* \rb into the city.|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb When Ruth returned|וַתָּבוֹא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb her mother-in-law,|חֲמוֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb Naomi asked her,|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “How did it go,|מִי־\rb*\rb |אַ֣תְּ\rb* \rb my daughter?”|בִּתִּ֑י\rb*
\p \rb Then Ruth told|וַתַּ֨גֶּד־\rb* \rb her|לָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Boaz|הָאִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb had done|עָֽשָׂה־\rb* \rb for her.|לָ֖הּ\rb* \v 17 \rb And she said,|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “He gave|נָ֣תַן\rb* \rb me|לִ֑י\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb six|שֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb measures of barley,|הַשְּׂעֹרִ֥ים\rb* \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb he said,|אָמַ֣רֵַ֔\rb* \rb ‘Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb go back|תָּב֥וֹאִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your mother-in-law|חֲמוֹתֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb empty-handed.’”|רֵיקָ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb “Wait,|שְׁבִ֣י\rb* \rb my daughter,”|בִתִּ֔י\rb* \rb said Naomi,|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “until|עַ֚ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you find out|תֵּֽדְעִ֔ין\rb* \rb how|אֵ֖יךְ\rb* \rb things|דָּבָ֑ר\rb* \rb go,|יִפֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb rest|יִשְׁקֹט֙\rb* \rb unless|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb he has resolved|כִּלָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the matter|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb today.”|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*
\c 4
\s1 Boaz Redeems Ruth
\p \v 1 \rb Meanwhile, Boaz|וּבֹ֨עַז\rb* \rb went|עָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb to the gate|הַשַּׁעַר֮\rb* \rb and sat down|וַיֵּ֣שֶׁב\rb* \rb there.|שָׁם֒\rb* \rb Soon|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb the kinsman-redeemer|הַגֹּאֵ֤ל\rb*\f + \fr 4:1 \ft The Hebrew word for \fqa kinsman-redeemer \ft or \fqa guardian-redeemer\ft is a legal term for the kinsman who redeems or vindicates a relative; also in verses 3, 6, 8, and 14; see \ref Leviticus 25:25–55|LEV 25:25-55\ref*.\f* \rb of whom he|בֹּ֔עַז\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּר־\rb* \rb came along,|עֹבֵר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb and Boaz said,|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb “Come over|ס֥וּרָה\rb* \rb here,|פֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb my friend,|פְּלֹנִ֣י\rb*\rb |אַלְמֹנִ֑י\rb* \rb and sit down.”|שְׁבָה־\rb* \rb So he went over|וַיָּ֖סַר\rb* \rb and sat down.|וַיֵּשֵֽׁב׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Then Boaz took|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֛ים\rb* \rb of the elders|מִזִּקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Sit|שְׁבוּ־\rb* \rb here,”|פֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and they did so.|וַיֵּשֵֽׁבוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb And he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to the kinsman-redeemer,|לַגֹּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb “Naomi,|נָעֳמִ֔י\rb* \rb who has returned|הַשָּׁ֖בָה\rb* \rb from the land|מִשְּׂדֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of Moab,|מוֹאָֽב׃\rb* \rb is selling|מָכְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb the piece|חֶלְקַת֙\rb* \rb of land|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb belonged to our brother|לְאָחִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb Elimelech.|לֶאֱלִימֶ֑לֶךְ\rb* \v 4 \rb I|וַאֲנִ֨י\rb* \rb thought|אָמַ֜רְתִּי\rb* \rb I should inform|אֶגְלֶ֧ה\rb* \rb you|אָזְנְךָ֣\rb* \rb that|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb you may buy it back|קְ֠נֵה\rb* \rb in the presence of|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb those seated here|הַֽיֹּשְׁבִים֮\rb* \rb and in the presence of|וְנֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of my people.|עַמִּי֒\rb* \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you want to redeem it,|תִּגְאַל֙\rb* \rb do so.|גְּאָ֔ל\rb* \rb But if you|וְאִם־\rb*\f + \fr 4:4 \ft Many Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, Vulgate, and Syriac; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa he\f* \rb will not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb redeem it,|יִגְאַ֜ל\rb* \rb tell|הַגִּ֣ידָה\rb* \rb me|לִּ֗י\rb* \rb so I may know,|וְאֵדַע\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb there is no one|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb but you|זוּלָֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb to redeem it,|לִגְא֔וֹל\rb* \rb and I am|וְאָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb next after you.”|אַחֲרֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\p \rb “I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb will redeem it,”|אֶגְאָֽל׃\rb* \rb he replied.|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Then Boaz|בֹּ֔עַז\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “On the day|בְּיוֹם־\rb* \rb you buy|קְנוֹתְךָ֥\rb* \rb the land|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb Naomi|נָעֳמִ֑י\rb* \rb and also from|וּ֠מֵאֵת\rb* \rb Ruth|ר֣וּת\rb* \rb the Moabitess,|הַמּוֹאֲבִיָּ֤ה\rb* \rb you must also acquire|קָנִיתִי\rb* \rb the widow|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb of the deceased|הַמֵּת֙\rb* \rb in order to raise|לְהָקִ֥ים\rb* \rb up the name|שֵׁם־\rb* \rb of the deceased|הַמֵּ֖ת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his inheritance.”|נַחֲלָתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb The kinsman-redeemer|הַגֹּאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “I cannot|לֹ֤א\rb*\rb |אוּכַל֙\rb* \rb redeem it|לִגְאוֹל\rb* \rb myself,|לִ֔י\rb* \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb I would jeopardize|אַשְׁחִ֖ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my own inheritance.|נַחֲלָתִ֑י\rb* \rb Take my right of redemption,|גְּאֻלָּתִ֔י\rb*\rb |גְּאַל־\rb*\rb |לְךָ֤\rb*\rb |אַתָּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I cannot|לֹא־\rb*\rb |אוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb redeem it.”|לִגְאֹֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Now|וְזֹאת֩\rb* \rb in former times|לְפָנִ֨ים\rb* \rb in Israel,|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb the redemption|הַגְּאוּלָּ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb or exchange of property,|הַתְּמוּרָה֙\rb* \rb to make any|כָּל־\rb* \rb matter|דָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb legally binding|לְקַיֵּ֣ם\rb* \rb a man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb would remove|שָׁלַ֥ף\rb* \rb his sandal|נַעֲל֖וֹ\rb* \rb and give it|וְנָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb to the other party,|לְרֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and this was|וְזֹ֥את\rb* \rb a confirmation|הַתְּעוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Israel.|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 8 \rb So the kinsman-redeemer|הַגֹּאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb removed|וַיִּשְׁלֹ֖ף\rb* \rb his sandal|נַעֲלֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to Boaz,|לְבֹ֖עַז\rb* \rb “Buy it|קְנֵה־\rb* \rb for yourself.”|לָ֑ךְ\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb At this, Boaz|בֹּ֨עַז\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to the elders|לַזְּקֵנִ֜ים\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb “You|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb are witnesses|עֵדִ֤ים\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I am buying|קָנִ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from|מִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb Naomi|נָעֳמִֽי׃\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb belonged to Elimelech,|לֶֽאֱלִימֶ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Chilion,|לְכִלְי֖וֹן\rb* \rb and Mahlon.|וּמַחְל֑וֹן\rb* \v 10 \rb Moreover,|וְגַ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I have acquired|קָנִ֧יתִי\rb*\rb |לִ֣י\rb* \rb Ruth|ר֣וּת\rb* \rb the Moabitess,|הַמֹּאֲבִיָּה֩\rb* \rb Mahlon’s|מַחְל֜וֹן\rb* \rb widow,|אֵ֨שֶׁת\rb* \rb as my wife,|לְאִשָּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb to raise up|לְהָקִ֤ים\rb* \rb the name|שֵׁם־\rb* \rb of the deceased|הַמֵּת֙\rb* \rb through|עַל־\rb* \rb his inheritance,|נַ֣חֲלָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb so that his|הַמֵּ֛ת\rb* \rb name|שֵׁם־\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb disappear|יִכָּרֵ֧ת\rb* \rb from among|מֵעִ֥ם\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֖יו\rb* \rb or from the gate|וּמִשַּׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb of his home.|מְקוֹמ֑וֹ\rb* \rb You|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb are witnesses today.”|עֵדִ֥ים\rb*\rb |הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb “We are witnesses,”|עֵדִ֑ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמְר֜וּ\rb* \rb the elders|וְהַזְּקֵנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb at the gate.|בַּשַּׁ֛עַר\rb* \rb “May the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb make|יִתֵּן֩\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֜ה\rb* \rb entering|הַבָּאָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb your home|בֵּיתֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb like Rachel|כְּרָחֵ֤ל׀\rb* \rb and Leah,|וּכְלֵאָה֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb together built up|בָּנ֤וּ\rb*\rb |שְׁתֵּיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb May you be|וַעֲשֵׂה־\rb* \rb prosperous|חַ֣יִל\rb* \rb in Ephrathah|בְּאֶפְרָ֔תָה\rb* \rb and famous|וּקְרָא־\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֖ם\rb*\rb |בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb in Bethlehem.|לָֽחֶם׃\rb* \v 12 \rb And may your house|בֵֽיתְךָ֙\rb* \rb become|וִיהִ֤י\rb* \rb like the house|כְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Perez,|פֶּ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Tamar|תָמָ֖ר\rb* \rb bore|יָלְדָ֥ה\rb* \rb to Judah,|לִֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb because of|מִן־\rb* \rb the offspring|הַזֶּ֗רַע\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb will give|יִתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֔\rb* \rb by|מִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb young woman.”|הַֽנַּעֲרָ֖ה\rb*
\s1 Boaz Marries Ruth
\p \v 13 \rb So Boaz|בֹּ֤עַז\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb Ruth,|רוּת֙\rb* \rb and she became|וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb his|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb wife.|לְאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb And when he had relations with|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb her,|אֵלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb enabled|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb her|לָ֛הּ\rb* \rb to conceive,|הֵרָי֖וֹן\rb* \rb and she gave birth to|וַתֵּ֥לֶד\rb* \rb a son.|בֵּֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then the women|הַנָּשִׁים֙\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּאמַ֤רְנָה\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Naomi,|נָעֳמִ֔י\rb* \rb “Blessed be|בָּר֣וּךְ\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb who|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb has not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb left|הִשְׁבִּ֥ית\rb* \rb you|לָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb this day|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb without a kinsman-redeemer.|גֹּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb May his name|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb become famous|וְיִקָּרֵ֥א\rb* \rb in Israel.|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 15 \rb He will renew|וְהָ֤יָה\rb*\rb |לְמֵשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb your|לָךְ֙\rb* \rb life|נֶ֔פֶשׁ\rb* \rb and sustain you|וּלְכַלְכֵּ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in your old age.|שֵׂיבָתֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb your daughter-in-law,|כַלָּתֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb who|אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb loves|אֲהֵבַ֙תֶךְ֙\rb* \rb you and is better|ט֣וֹבָה\rb* \rb to you than|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb seven|מִשִּׁבְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb sons,|בָּנִֽים׃\rb* \rb has given him birth.”|יְלָדַ֔תּוּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |הִיא֙\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb And Naomi|נָעֳמִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb the child,|הַיֶּ֙לֶד֙\rb* \rb placed him|וַתְּשִׁתֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb on her lap,|בְחֵיקָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and became|וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb a nurse|לְאֹמֶֽנֶת׃\rb* \rb to him.|ל֖וֹ\rb* \v 17 \rb The neighbor|הַשְּׁכֵנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb women said,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “A son|בֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb has been born|יֻלַּד־\rb* \rb to Naomi,”|לְנָעֳמִ֑י\rb*\rb |וַתִּקְרֶ֤אנָֽה\rb*\rb |שְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb and they named|וַתִּקְרֶאנָה֩\rb* \rb him|ל֨וֹ\rb*\rb |שֵׁם֙\rb* \rb Obed.|עוֹבֵ֔ד\rb* \rb He became|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb the father|אֲבִי־\rb* \rb of Jesse,|יִשַׁ֖י\rb* \rb the father|אֲבִ֥י\rb* \rb of David.|דָוִֽד׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Line of David
\r \ref Matthew 1:1–17|MAT 1:1-17\ref*; \ref Luke 3:23–38|LUK 3:23-38\ref*)
\p \v 18 \rb Now these are|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb the generations|תּוֹלְד֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Perez:|פָּ֔רֶץ\rb*
\li1 \rb Perez|פֶּ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֥יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Hezron,|חֶצְרֽוֹן׃\rb*
\li1 \v 19 \rb Hezron|וְחֶצְרוֹן֙\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ram,|רָ֔ם\rb*
\li1 \rb Ram|וְרָ֖ם\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֥יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Amminadab,|עַמִּֽינָדָֽב׃\rb*
\li1 \v 20 \rb Amminadab|וְעַמִּֽינָדָב֙\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Nahshon,|נַחְשׁ֔וֹן\rb*
\li1 \rb Nahshon|וְנַחְשׁ֖וֹן\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֥יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Salmon,|שַׂלְמָֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 4:20 \ft A few Hebrew manuscripts, some LXX manuscripts, and Vulgate (see also verse 21 and LXX of \ref 1 Chronicles 2:11|1CH 2:11\ref*); most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Salma\f*
\li1 \v 21 \rb Salmon|וְשַׂלְמוֹן֙\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Boaz,|בֹּ֔עַז\rb*
\li1 \rb Boaz|וּבֹ֖עַז\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֥יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Obed,|עוֹבֵֽד׃\rb*
\li1 \v 22 \rb Obed|וְעֹבֵד֙\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֣יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jesse,|יִשָׁ֔י\rb*
\li1 \rb and Jesse|וְיִשַׁ֖י\rb* \rb was the father of|הוֹלִ֥יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David.|דָּוִֽד׃\rb*
